The   driver   provides  support  for  the  Microchip  Technology
MCP9805/98242 and other chips that conform to JEDEC Standard 21‐C
section 4.7.  Memory module temperature sensors are  optional  on
DDR2 and newer DIMMs.  Sensors provided by this driver, including
the  on‐chip  thresholds for the Alarm Window and Critical level,
are accessed through the API.  The  supports  temperature  ranges
from  ‐256  to +255 degrees C.  Chips supported by the driver in‐
clude TSE2004av compliant devices and: Analog Devices ADT7408 At‐
mel  AT30TS00  and   AT30TSE004   On   semiconductor   (Catalyst)
CAT34TS02,  CAT34TS02C, CAT34TS04 and CAT6095 Giantec Semiconduc‐
tor  GT30TS00  and   GT34TS02   Integrated   Deviced   Technology
TSE2002B3,    TSE2002GB2,    TSE2004GB2,   TS3000B3,   TS3000GB0,
TS3000GB2, and  TS30001GB2  Maxim  MAX6604  Microchip  Technology
EMC1501,  MCP9804,  MCP9805,  MCP9843,  MCP98242,  MCP98243,  and
MCP98244 NXP  Semiconductors  SE97  and  SE98  STmicroelectronics
STTS424,  STTS424E,  STTS2002,  STTS2004, and STTS3000 The device
appeared in Interrupt support is unimplemented.
